call.raw_text:
{
  "workers": [
    {
      "worker": 1,
      "brief": "You are given a slice of the ledger containing rows 11‑20. For each line item, determine the unit rate: if the unit_rate column is non‑empty use it, otherwise look up the rate_code in the rate table (rows 1‑10). Compute amount_owed = qty × unit_rate. If paid < amount_owed, report the line as UNDERPAID with the shortfall (amount_owed – paid) rounded to two decimals. Do NOT report lines that are exactly paid or overpaid. Output a JSON array of objects with fields: row, line_id, claim_id, shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[11, 20]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 2,
      "brief": "You are given rows 21‑30. Perform the same underpayment analysis as described for Worker 1. Report each underpaid line with its shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[21, 30]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 3,
      "brief": "You are given rows 31‑40. Perform the same underpayment analysis as described for Worker 1. Report each underpaid line with its shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[31, 40]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 4,
      "brief": "You are given rows 41‑50. Perform the same underpayment analysis as described for Worker 1. Report each underpaid line with its shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[41, 50]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 5,
      "brief": "You are given rows 51‑60. Perform the same underpayment analysis as described for Worker 1. Report each underpaid line with its shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[51, 60]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 6,
      "brief": "You are given rows 61‑70. Perform the same underpayment analysis as described for Worker 1. Report each underpaid line with its shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[61, 70]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 7,
      "brief": "You are given rows 1‑10 (the rate table). No underpayment analysis is needed. Just return the rate_code to unit_rate mapping as a JSON object, e.g., {\"RC1\": 12.34, \"RC2\": 5.67, ...}. This will be used by other workers to resolve rate codes.",
      "ranges": [[1, 10]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 8,
      "brief": "You have the full ledger rows 1‑70. Using the rate table (rows 1‑10) and all line items (rows 11‑70), identify every claim_id that appears on more than one line item. For each duplicated claim_id, list all row numbers where it occurs. Output a JSON array of objects with fields: claim_id, rows (array of row numbers, sorted ascending). Do NOT include claim_ids that appear only once.",
      "ranges": [[1, 70]]
    }
  ]
}

call.prompt:
You are auditing a remittance ledger with two sections. The rate table lists rate codes and their unit rates. Each line item is one billed service; it gives either its own unit_rate or a rate_code whose unit rate is in the rate table. The amount owed for a line is qty x unit rate. A line is UNDERPAID when paid is less than the amount owed; its shortfall is (amount owed) - paid, in currency units with two decimals. Lines paid exactly, or overpaid, are not underpayments and must not be reported as underpaid. A claim is DUPLICATED when the same claim_id appears on more than one line item (billed more than once). Find every underpaid line and every duplicated claim.

8 workers each checked part of the ledger. You do not see the ledger. Their reports:
Worker 1: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}
Worker 2: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "RX-ZMKAD", "shortfall": 420.4}], "duplicates": []}
Worker 3: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "RX-PNK47", "shortfall": 215.17}], "duplicates": []}
Worker 4: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "RX-MZ572", "shortfall": 622.85}], "duplicates": []}
Worker 5: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "RX-C9TVB", "shortfall": 324.22}], "duplicates": [{"line_ids": ["RX-95H9X", "RX-B7SN9"]}]}
Worker 6: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}
Worker 7: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}
Worker 8: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}

Produce the final report.
Do not show your working or any explanation. Reply with only a JSON object: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "<line_id>", "shortfall": <amount with two decimals>}], "duplicates": [{"line_ids": ["<line_id>", "<line_id>"]}]}. List only lines whose shortfall is greater than 0. Use empty lists if there are none.
